Package: pinyin-ime
Architecture: any
Depends: libimecore0, libimepinyin0, fcitx5, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Linux pinyin input method based on libime
 pinyin-ime is a Linux pinyin input method engine based on libime.
 It provides both a command-line interface (pinyin_ime_cli) and a
 Fcitx5 addon (libpinyinime.so) for system-level input.
 .
 Features:
  * Full pinyin, simplified pinyin, fuzzy pinyin
  * Double pinyin (8 schemes: Xiaohe/Ziranma/MS/Ziguang/ABC/...)
  * User language model with self-learning
  * Chinese/English switching, Chinese punctuation
  * Emoji input, cursor movement, undo
  * M3 correction module (CHIME + bigram transition)

Package: pinyin-ime-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: libimecore0, libimepinyin0, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Command-line pinyin input method (standalone CLI)
 Standalone command-line interface for pinyin-ime, without fcitx5 dependency.
 Useful for testing, scripting, and headless environments.
 .
 Features: full/simplified/fuzzy/double pinyin, user learning,
 batch mode, JSON output, accuracy evaluation.
